Hi [~accountid:5d8df26dc26b6a0dcb0d0cb4] 

We have received a response from SilverFlow. All of the error messages originate from the issuer bank. 
The causes for the error messages can be quite vague and vary a lot. 
I will follow up with SilverFlow to see if there are any actions we could take to reduce the amount of refund fraud error messages. 

{{Below you can find some common scenarios for response code 59 for refunds:}}

* {{Unusual refund patterns or amounts}}
* {{Refunds to cards that have been flagged for suspicious activity}}
* {{Refunds that don't match typical merchant behavior patterns}}
* {{Cross-border refund transactions that trigger geographic risk rules}}
* {{Refunds processed outside normal business hours or patterns}}
* {{Multiple refund attempts in short time periods}}

{{The issuer's fraud detection system analyses various risk factors and if the refund transaction is deemed suspicious but not definitively fraudulent, response code 59 is the appropriate decline code to use.All the examples I could find come from Portugese Banks (Novo Banco and Banco Comercial Portugues)}}

