Thanks [~accountid:63f742e4e8216251ae4e4ef6] - in which case, I have made some minor tweaks to the DSA which is otherwise fine to share with MOL.

To make all of my advice to date easier to track, I summarise it all below in this comment.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
# *Data Sharing Agreement*
{panel}

I have no comments on the _Partnership Agreement_ from a privacy POV (/) 

However, per Clause 11.3 of the Partnership Agreement, if any driver personal data is being shared (which is the case here, as we are sharing Bolt driver MOL Move Card Numbers with MOL), we should ensure that we enter into a Data Sharing Agreement with MOL. I have prepared a draft here ([+*link*+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1d006x5TH0THqbMxCZycyvJ1Yrv8gPpRlVjKmQNvop_M/edit?tab=t.0]), which can be shared with MOL for review.

It is generally advisable to enter into a DSA whenever Bolt is sharing user personal data with third parties, as this ensures that Bolt is protected in case the third party’s non-compliance / data breaches result in any liability for Bolt. As such, let’s see what MOL has to say about the DSA. If, however, MOL pushes back strongly on this DSA, please note that it is *_not a deal-breaker_*, given that the data at-issue here is very low risk. As such, although we should push for the DSA, it should not act as a blocker to entering into the relationship with MOL.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
# *Promotional Comms*
{panel}

Posting the MOL offer on the Bolt Rewards Page does not raise any material direct marketing issues, and so I have no concerns from a privacy POV (/)

With regards to sending *push notifications* to drivers about the MOL services, this is caught by direct marketing rules. As such, these notifications *should only be sent to drivers that have consented / opted-in to receiving them* (i.e., drivers that have consented to ‘partner offers’ on their account) (!) 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
# *Bolt Form for collecting driver details* ([+link+|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1UEDaPSFypCMmb7ZcDstwe76ux9r5L7EusXMllj0xo0Y/edit])
{panel}

We should {color:#ff5630}*avoid collecting the driver’s consent*{color} in this form (!) This is because if we rely on consent as the legal basis for sharing, and then the driver withdraws that consent (which thy are allowed to do at any time), then we will be prevented from sharing the data, which in turn could create operational friction. Instead, we can rely on _legitimate interest_ as our legal basis for sharing the data.

In terms of what this means practically for the form, please could you:

* Remove the paragraph on collecting consent, as well as the tickbox.
* Instead, translate and include the following disclaimer language (either at the start or the end of the form - wherever is easiest: “_If you provide your MOL Move Card Number via this form, Bolt will share it with MOL Polska sp. z o.o. (and its affiliated companies) based on Bolt’s legitimate interest in facilitating your participation in the Bolt Rewards Programme and measuring its effectiveness. For more information on your rights and the processing of your personal data, please refer to our privacy notice available at_ [https://bolt.eu/pl-pl/privacy/global-privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/pl-pl/privacy/global-privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides|smart-link] _._”

