{quote}# Do we have an exact *number of unique individuals* whose documents were attached to the dummy vehicle (ID: 7748919)?{quote}

Not an exact number. As an estimate, there are three different document types attached to the dummy car, so there are likely up to 3 documents per individual, so approximately 2443 / 3 = 815 individuals. As it’s a dummy car, it seems unlikely that the same individual would upload documents more than once. If an exact number is needed, I can try to figure it out, but it would take some effort to track where exactly all the documents came from.

{quote}# What exact *documents are assigned* to the dummy vehicle?{quote}

The car in question has three document types associated with it: Vehicle Inspection Report (za_car_inspection), License Disc & Roadworthy Certificate Disc (za_car_license_disc), Operator Card Disc (za_car_operator_card_disc). Examples can be accessed from the documents tab in the Admin Panel car page.

{quote}# Are there any *indications that other drivers' exports* may have included documents from this or other dummy vehicles previously?{quote}

May have, certainly, but we have no good way of checking this that I know of. The possibility has been there since automatic data exports were implemented, and if the export ran into no technical issues, we would not be aware of it. Note that this applies not only to dummy cars, but any other cars that have been used by more than one driver (e.g. fleet cars).

{quote}# Who from the Data Team is assessing whether the *affected export file (ID: 788571)* has been *accessed or downloaded* by the Driver who requested the data export?{quote}

Łukasz Wołodkiewicz was handling it ([slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06RUSHTRA4/p1754485843432949]). However, the conclusion seems to be that we have insufficient tracking, so we can’t tell.

{quote}# If the export has not been downloaded yet, is the conclusion that we can stop the download attempt, or is it too late?{quote}

Łukasz Wołodkiewicz removed the possibility to download the export, so if it wasn’t yet downloaded, then it will not be possible to download it in the future, but as per above, we can’t tell whether it was already downloaded or not.

{quote}# Apart from dummy car 7748919, are *any other dummy vehicles known to have high document loads* that might present a similar risk?{quote}

I was told that there is a dummy car per city for ZA, and possibly similar cars are used in other markets as well, although not all of them have a high document load at the moment. A quick search for cars with the registration number ADD_YOUR_CAR gives 166 cars (both active and deleted), some of them have no/few documents, but at least some have quite a few, for example [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/cars/car/8937334|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/cars/car/8937334], [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/cars/car/7318404|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/cars/car/7318404]

