Yes, Section 4 (Production Order) and Section 5 (Urgent Demand) of the Missing Persons Act, 2018 (Ontario) are valid legal bases for Bolt to disclose data to police without user consent, provided the request is made in accordance with the Act.

What I mean by in accordance with the Act:
Section 4:

The request must be authorized by a justice of the peace or judge, and the following conditions must be met:

# A missing person investigation is underway;
# The police officer has reasonable grounds to believe the person’s safety is at risk;
# The information sought may assist in locating the person;
# The order is served properly on the organization holding the data.

Section 5: 
The police may bypass the court only if:

# There are reasonable grounds to believe the person’s safety is at risk, and
# The situation is urgent — waiting for a production order could cause harm;
# The demand is made in writing, includes specific records, and outlines the grounds for urgency;
# The officer has reasonable belief that the organization controls the relevant information.

