* this agreement is crucial from the perspective of Bolt’s operations, so it is important for Bolt to have the most important obligations secured;
* the MSA does not include any contractual penalties itself, but rather regulates the rules for their execution and enforcement;
* the way Clause 8 in Schedule 2 is drafted, it also protects the Service Provider in case of Bolt committed the breaches, so it is actually beneficial to them too; 
* the scope of the contractual penalties is defined and limited - it relates to critical issues (IP, security or confidentiality breaches, non-compliance with laws);
* the proposal is well-balanced - it ensures the same contractual penalty amount and cap for both parties.

Hope this helps. In case of further questions please let me know.

